<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright (c) 2026, NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES. All rights reserved.
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

The entitlements a confined plugin host is signed with.

App Sandbox is deny-by-default: a signed bundle carrying only this entitlement
reaches its own container and what it was handed, and no user files, no devices,
no outbound network. There is deliberately no `com.apple.security.*` resource
entitlement here — a host that needs one is a host whose plugin needs a
capability, and capabilities are granted by the runtime rather than by widening
the bundle every plugin runs inside.

Library validation stays ON in this variant, so a plugin is loadable only when it
is signed by Apple or by this bundle's own team. The variant for plugins signed
by somebody else is `nemo-plugin-host-restricted-third-party.plist`, and the
weakening it carries is the reason it is a separate file.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
